  "research_id": "dtcc-tokenization-2026",
  "title": "DTCC Tokenization and Settlement — 2026",
  "question": "What has DTCC actually built with tokens, what did the July 15 production event prove, and what would faster settlement do to cash and collateral?",
  "bluf": "DTCC's tokenization is a controlled layer beside the old system, not a new market. DTC's first tokens move no cash and count for zero in DTC's collateral and settlement checks; Cede & Co. stays the registered owner, DTC's LedgerScan is the official record, and DTC can mint, burn, move or correct tokens. Limited production workflows ran on July 15, 2026. Collateral AppChain is an expected launch, not a live system, and DTCC has not published an auditable model for the capital and liquidity savings it claims. Moving from netted to instant one-for-one settlement would require prefunding cash that netting now saves.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-08-21",
  "evidence_cutoff_note": "Core studies as of August 2; the notice and testing calendar as of August 21.",
